From 8a1268041619b03ef685c2eac9d610835cdcde00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:45:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/15] Round 6: Reuse per-worker scratch buffers across
 candidates

Move the kernel's and verifier's per-candidate buffers into a
domain::Scratch that the inline caller or each worker creates once per
batch and resets per candidate. Build the delay vector only for
metrics; the score adds the same terms in the same order. The
randomized tests reuse one scratch across all models.

Workload: serial in matrix mode (96 example candidates), 11 samples.
Before median: 0.101 ms. After median: 0.060 ms. Speedup: 1.67x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
